[5] Candidate proof statement
  Endpoint-owner transfer lemma target:
    Inside the protected strict-open B18Z6 residual surface, the external
    endpoint-owner strip is a non-route local address.  It refines exact-M
    and coarse-topology capacitor cuts, splits the q=23 diagonal, and can
    be joined with the largest-safe-component owner stalk before falling
    back to full packet labels.
  Current finite evidence:
    all four residual capacitor packets have endpoint_current_word=B18Z6;
    external owner strips split both residual pairs and distinguish petal,
    K33, q=23 covering, and single-swap covering packets.
  Guardrail:
    coarse B/Z endpoint counts are diagnostics only.  A proof quotient must
    retain owner names, reconstruct them, annihilate them by a dual
    certificate, or route the lost coordinate to named residual debt.
